blisher.","text":"Terms of use\nRawThoughts Enterprises Private Limited (RTEPL) publishes and operates RawThoughts, Causality, Sleepwalker and Post-AGI Economics. These terms concern your use of rawthoughts.in, causality.in, sleepwalker.in and post-agi-economics.org, and of every subdomain of them, such as the documentation at docs.rawthoughts.in and docs.causality.in.\nReading and reusing material\nUnless a page states its own licence, the content of these four publications, their text, images and data, is not openly licensed. You may read it, link to its pages and quote passages from it with attribution: name the author or publication and link to the page you quote. We permit that use, and it leaves untouched any wider right you have under fair dealing (section 52 of India's Copyright Act, 1957) or fair use elsewhere. The permission covers accurate quotation only; it does not cover misquoting the material or quoting it out of context so that it says something it does not. Reproducing the material without attribution, or presenting it as your own, is not permitted.\nSearch engines and answer systems may read these pages and cite them with attribution and a link. The crawler rules state the access preferences for this site. We reserve the use of this material for AI model training, wherever copies are collected from these websites, their subdomains or another source. This reservation is also our opt-out from text and data mining wherever the law provides one. The reservation leaves existing licences and third-party rights intact. The documentation hosts publish their own crawler rules for RawThoughts docs and Causality docs.\nFor other copying, adaptation or redistribution, follow the licence attached to the page, asset or source, or ask us or the rights holder named on the item. Attribution alone does not replace permission.\nAuthors, contributors and third parties retain the rights attributed to them. Quotations, translations, images and software do not acquire a common licence merely by appearing on this website. A software repository's licence governs that software, not all the prose or images published here.\nThe scope of the publication\nThe publications cover applied ideas, economic inquiry, research and creative work. Read a research model with its stated assumptions and limits; its description does not guarantee how a deployed system will perform. Economic arguments and scenarios offer neither personal investment, tax or financial advice nor a transaction or guaranteed forecast. Interpretations of source texts, fiction and artistic experiments should be read in that form, rather than taken as medical guidance or scientific findings.\nConsulting work, software use, support and service levels follow their own agreements. Reading these pages or sending an enquiry does not enter you into one. Software, datasets, source texts, translations and contributed works keep their own licences and rights.\nWe aim to keep the material accurate and correct errors brought to our attention. Sources, methods and circumstances can change; a dated account concerns the setting it describes. You remain responsible for assessing whether material is suitable for your circumstances and for seeking qualified advice where needed.\nResponsible use\nDo not use the website to infringe another person's rights, expose confidential information, impersonate someone, interfere with its operation or attempt unauthorised access.\nExternal websites and services have their own terms. A reference is not an assurance of their accuracy, security or continued availability.\nAvailability and responsibility\nThe publication is provided as information. We do not promise uninterrupted access or that every example will suit a particular purpose. To the extent permitted by applicable law, we make no warranty of fitness for your use and are not responsible for loss arising from reliance on the material or interruption of access. Nothing here excludes a responsibility or remedy that the law does not allow us to exclude.\nPrivacy and contact\nThe privacy notice explains the information handled by this publication’s website and reading tools. A new use requiring consent will ask for it; continued reading is not agreement to that use.\nFor a correction, permission request or concern about these terms, write to info@rtepl.co.in. Please identify the page and the issue so we can respond.\nGoverning law\nIndian law governs these terms. Subject to mandatory law and any jurisdiction that cannot lawfully be excluded, disputes concerning use of the website fall within the jurisdiction of the competent courts in Lucknow. These terms do not replace a separate contract, licence or statutory right.\n","url":"https://causality.in/terms/","publisher":{"@id":"https://rawthoughts.in/#organization","identifier":"organization:rtepl","@type":"Organization","name":"RawThoughts Enterprises Private Limited","url":"https://rawthoughts.in/","sameAs":[{"@id":"https://github.com/getHarshOnline"}]}},{"@context":{"@version":1.1,"@vocab":"https://schema.org/","url":{"@id":"https://schema.org/url","@type":"@id"}},"@id":"https://causality.in/blog/oldest/","@type":"CollectionPage","creativeWorkStatus":"published","description":"Worked questions about distinctions, causal evidence and learning under limits.","http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasGeneratedBy":{"@type":"http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Activity","http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#used":[{"@id":"https://rawthoughts.in/gazette/"},{"@id":"https://github.com/getHarshOnline/gazette-theme-lattice"}]},"identifier":"collection:causality-essays","inLanguage":"en","mainEntity":{"@type":"ItemList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","item":{"@id":"https://causality.in/blog/the-ineffable-geometry/#article","identifier":"content:causality-the-ineffable-geometry","name":"The ineffable geometry","url":"https://causality.in/blog/the-ineffable-geometry/"},"position":1},{"@type":"ListItem","item":{"@id":"https://causality.in/blog/entropy